   "reply": "The command that works, run from the project root:\n\n```\nPYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests -v\n```\n\nBoth tests passed (`test_transfer_preserves_total` and `test_rejects_non_positive_amount`).\n\n- **Why `PYTHONPATH=src`:** the package is under `src/ledgerlite`, and it isn't installed. Without that setting, `from ledgerlite import Ledger` won't resolve.\n- **Why `unittest`:** the tests use it, and pytest isn't installed. `python -m pytest` fails with \"No module named pytest\".\n\nIn PowerShell or cmd, set the variable separately first: `set PYTHONPATH=src` in cmd, or `$env:PYTHONPATH=\"src\"` in PowerShell.",
